<%# locals(user:, product_name:) -%>
<%#
  Pre-purchase notice shown to India RBI customers (those whose account has automatic card payments
  disabled by RBI regulations) when the synchronous manual-payment finalization flow is enabled. It
  sets the expectation that, after subscribing, they'll be guided to manually authorize a one-time
  payment to activate their subscription, so the redirect to the "Pay your bill" page that follows a
  declined advance payment doesn't read like an error. Renders nothing for everyone else, and is
  suppressed once the customer is back on this page with the payment-processing banner showing.
-%>
<% if user.autopay_disabled_by_india_rbi? && FeatureFlag.vexi.enabled?(:copilot_rbi_manual_payment_signup, user, default: false) && params[Billing::ManualPaymentRedirect::PAYMENT_PROCESSING_PARAM].blank? %>
  <%= render(Primer::Alpha::Banner.new(
    icon: :info,
    scheme: :default,
    test_selector: "rbi-manual-payment-notice",
    classes: "tmp-mb-4",
  )) do %>
    <strong>One extra step to activate your <%= product_name %> subscription.</strong>
    Under Reserve Bank of India (RBI) regulations, automatic card payments are disabled on your account.
    After you subscribe, we'll take you to a secure page to authorize a one-time payment. Once it's
    confirmed, we'll finish setting up your subscription. This usually only takes a moment.
  <% end %>
<% end %>

